6. Explain terraform project directory structure ?

main.tf → Main file to define resources and infrastructure logic

variables.tf → File to define input variables (structure only)

terraform.tfvars → File to assign values to variables

outputs.tf → File to define output values after execution

provider.tf → File to define cloud providers (AWS, Azure, etc.)

backend.tf → File to configure remote state storage (S3, Azure Blob, etc.)

versions.tf → File to define required Terraform and provider versions

✅ Modules
modules/ → Directory to store reusable Terraform code

modules/vpc/main.tf → Defines VPC resources inside module

modules/vpc/variables.tf → Defines inputs for module

modules/vpc/outputs.tf → Returns outputs from module

✅ Auto-generated Files

.terraform/ → Stores downloaded providers and modules

terraform.tfstate → Stores current infrastructure state (most important)

terraform.tfstate.backup → Backup of state file

.terraform.lock.hcl → Locks provider versions for consistency

